WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.459 --> 00:00:05.500
Music producer Tomas de Niero urgently needs
a new kidney.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.650
And it's not the first time.

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:11.650
He had a transplant 14 years ago when both
his own kidneys failed.

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:15.130
He was already living on the Spanish island
of Mallorca at the time.

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:18.280
And that might have saved his life.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.849
"It was pure luck.

00:00:20.849 --> 00:00:23.839
I emigrated to Spain in 2001.

00:00:23.839 --> 00:00:27.659
And then two years later, when my kidneys
failed, I was in a country where you can get

00:00:27.659 --> 00:00:31.029
kidneys four or five times faster than in
Germany.

00:00:31.029 --> 00:00:34.469
It was pure luck!"

00:00:34.469 --> 00:00:38.680
He's hoping this time he'll also get a new
kidney without too much delay, because in

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:44.519
Spain, more people donate organs after they
die than anywhere else in the world.

00:00:44.519 --> 00:00:50.699
That's because by law, everyone there is automatically
an organ donor unless they actively opt out.

00:00:50.699 --> 00:00:52.829
It's a well-organized system.

00:00:52.829 --> 00:00:59.719
For the moment, Tomas still has to have to
have peritoneal dialysis every day.

00:00:59.719 --> 00:01:04.019
It takes hours, and limits his activities
dramatically.

00:01:04.019 --> 00:01:08.000
He'd have to wait about eight years on average
in Germany for a new kidney.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.159
In Spain, the waiting list is just two years
long.

00:01:11.159 --> 00:01:15.920
Reason enough for some to try to fiddle the
system:

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:20.840
"Some Germans are now declaring that they
live in Spain.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:25.270
I know two or three who've created a pretend
life here...buying houses, setting up small

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:32.289
firms...all so they can benefit from the Spanish
healthcare system."

00:01:32.289 --> 00:01:36.329
Miguel Ángel Feriol had a liver transplant
10 years ago.

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:39.310
Today, he's back in good shape.

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:44.869
Miguel has a problem with people coming from
abroad just to benefit from the Spanish system...although

00:01:44.869 --> 00:01:50.469
he also sympathizes:
"I can't imagine what it must be like to have

00:01:50.469 --> 00:01:52.020
wait for so many years.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:53.680
I know what waiting means.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:54.740
It's not a life.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:58.630
But for me it went by fast.

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:00.970
."
Miguel understands the need.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:06.460
But he also regrets that the rise in transplant
tourism means that people who really do live

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:14.130
in Spain will have to wait longer for a donor
organ.

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:18.030
"Spaniards donate their organs for people
in Spain.

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:23.860
Of course, we know that an organ -- a liver,
a kidney -- might be sent elsewhere if it's

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:25.840
not needed here.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:30.610
But if more and more people come here for
transplants, then this will have to be stopped.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:34.910
That's the only thing that makes sense."

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:39.940
Transplant tourism is technically banned in
the EU, but it's also difficult to control.

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:45.270
Many kidney transplants are carried out at
the university hospital in Palma de Mallorca.

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:48.860
The senior consultant here has operated on
many Germans.

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:50.690
He treats anybody with a need.

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:55.270
It's not his job to determine whether a foreigner
actually lives in Spain, or just pretends

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:59.840
to in order to benefit from the system.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:03.710
"There's freedom of movement in the EU.

00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:06.520
So it's hard to distinguish.

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:11.890
That's why the authorities have to ensure
there's order, and why they have to set clear

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:17.590
rules."

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:20.180
The pressure is rising.

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:24.200
Now the National Transplant Organization at
the Spanish health ministry has developed

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:27.500
new criteria for foreign patients.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:31.380
In the future, only people who have lived
in Spain for a minimum of two years will be

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:35.160
eligible to receive organs.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:40.670
"We have to check things much more closely.

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:44.060
Only people who have a lot of money can pretend
to be living here.

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:48.110
People with less fall by the wayside, and
have to wait longer in their own countries

00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:55.790
for an organ donation."

00:03:55.790 --> 00:04:01.610
Tomas de Niero can't understand why there
aren't more organ donors in Germany.

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:06.180
He blames a lack of coordination, and the
fact that you have to expressly state that

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.880
you want to donate your organs when you die.

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:15.080
"It's terrible that people from Germany are
going abroad -- even to India -- to get an

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:20.000
organ they can't get at home because of a
dumb rule, which really needs to be changed

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:24.620
now."

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:28.169
Everyone who dies on Spanish soil is a potential
organ donor.

00:04:28.169 --> 00:04:29.539
So who knows?

00:04:29.539 --> 00:04:34.139
One day, a German tourist could be the one
to save Tomas de Niero's life.

